  {
   "id": "orbit-industries-194457@1.2.10713.0",
   "gameId": "orbit-industries-194457",
   "displayName": "PATCH 1.2.10713.0",
   "kind": "patch",
   "kindBasis": "studio",
   "announcedAt": "2025-07-14T18:56:35.000Z",
   "notes": [
    {
     "title": "Hello Engineers, Space Pioneers, and Optimization Enthusiasts,",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "We’re thrilled to share two exciting updates with you today: orbit.industries is part of the Steam Automation Fest, and we’ve just launched a brand-new Patch!",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "[img src=\"{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41048672/4cd65b476148dee049ea277941e49b4a85c50edf.png\"]",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "🚀 Steam Automation Fest",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "orbit.industries is featured alongside other standout titles in this year’s Steam Automation Fest — a celebration of games that challenge you to automate, optimize, and streamline… like managing a space station!",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "[img src=\"{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/41048672/b46ef7551dea0c396537e7e4226311fa42214a89.png\"]",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "⚙️Patch 1.2.10713.0",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "A new patch appeared on the orbit with a couple of QoL changes and bug fixes!",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "Now, in a Station Management Interface, you can re-read tutorial texts if you missed something!",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "Moreover, Tabs in the Station Management Interface (SMI) now remember which group or sub-menu was expanded last.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "QoL improvements",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Include the possibility to re-read tutorial texts in SMI",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "new"
      },
      {
       "text": "Add a label to the x-axis of charts in Station Overview (SMI)",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "new"
      },
      {
       "text": "Do not repeat spoken station reports from AI if the in-game time is paused",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "new"
      },
      {
       "text": "Settings - Let players manually adjust the UI scale and font size",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "new"
      },
      {
       "text": "Settings - Include option to mute game audio when tabbing out of the game",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "new"
      },
      {
       "text": "Tabs in SMI should remember which group was expanded last",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "new"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Bugfixes",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Spoken language of A.I. buddy sometimes isn't correct (there was a bug that had it talking in English even when another language was selected in the menu)",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "fixed"
      },
      {
       "text": "In build mode (External Station View | ESV), the displayed rotation of new modules should now be correct, and modules should be placeable if no collision is detected (there was a bug in the rotation of preview modules, so players thought they could build a module when in fact there was a collision)",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "fixed"
      },
      {
       "text": "Undeployed systems in the Abstract System Layer (ASL) shouldn't stick to the mouse cursor anymore when expanding or closing the system overview",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": true,
       "category": "fixed",
       "platforms": [
        "pc"
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "Let us know how the current changes work for you, and stay tuned for the next updates!",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "fixed"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
